Yeah, and the places where you really care about conflict+free action
(sanctum/planes) are no teleport anyway so as long as you remember to
put telecontrol back on when leaving the Sanctum you're fine.

P and R don't warrant genocide (I'd do ; before either of them for
ease of running around Water).  Especially h is nice to have gone
before Rodney's on your tail summoning things (makes the travel
commands safer, which saves some tedium).

Def. uncurse the bell, I'd uncurse the /death too.

Don't bother fixing the pickaxe, if it bothers you you could go grab a
fresh one but you're probably done using it.  I'd be ditching it for
weight right about now (grab a few /digging for Earth).

> More /oDeath and /oPoly

/teleport are more important, IMO.  One decently charged /death is
usually fine though 2 is nice.  /poly are a bit fun for air elementals
but certainly not required.

> She's got Fire Brand and Frost Brand stashed by an alter.  Would one
> these be better than Mjollnir?  Would it be worth it attempt to get
> another artifact weapon from an alter?

You don't need to bother repairing/fooproofing the armor, your AC is
fine and you'll be enchanting some boots.  If you stumble upon a bunch
of scrolls that's nice, but not a big deal.

Fire Brand will be better than Mojo on the run (less stuff resists it
on Astral/Air, and it does more damage against stuff that resists
it).

#twoweapon does ridiculous amounts of damage, (even more once the off-
hand weapon is enchated up).
You should ditch the shield (you have SDSM) and #twoweapon with a
katana, or longsword (silver saber is common but you're past most of
the stuff where it helps a lot, and katana (preferred) or longsword
will be better in the Sanctum/Planes).

You should get jumping boots and remember to use them (liberally on
Sanctum/Astral), or get speed boots.  Remember you need light to
jump.  Either way, echant the boots up.

You should remember to use conflict liberally, especially in the
Sanctum/Air/Astral.  I'd leave it on unless I need my =levitate (may
not apply if you're relying on lev boots, in which case leave it on
always).  It also helps deal with satiation problems.

Consider using the spoily controlled levelport means of skipping some
stuff, though I'd want to do it all at least once.

